      "content": "If you cannot deny the vote, agencies that deny facts often lose more credibility than those who acknowledge minor past errors; a strategic approach is to frame the vote as a narrow compromise aimed at broader community needs while emphasizing the candidate's subsequent actions supporting the center's operations. Have the campaign team prepare a concise, factual statement that acknowledges the historical record without over-apologizing, then pivot immediately to current performance and future policy proposals to address the immediate media narrative. Finally, instruct your spokesperson to avoid engaging in endless debates on the specific bill details, instead keeping media interactions focused on the candidate's current approval ratings and campaign goals to mitigate damage before the primary.",
